{
  "duration": 82.299,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.639,
      "end": 1.459,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.2,
      "end": 3.799,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.179,
      "end": 7.359,
      "text": "In this problem, we are given that sine theta plus cos theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.899,
      "end": 9.779,
      "text": "is equal to seven by five,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.079,
      "end": 12.399,
      "text": "and we need to find sine theta into cos theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.779,
      "end": 16.779,
      "text": "Now, whenever we see sine theta plus cos theta together, there is one very useful trick."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.119,
      "end": 18.279,
      "text": "We square both sides."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.079,
      "end": 24.099,
      "text": "So sine theta plus cos theta whole square is equal to seven by five whole square."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.6,
      "end": 25.939,
      "text": "After opening the bracket,"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.359,
      "end": 27.84,
      "text": "this becomes sine square theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.279,
      "end": 31.999,
      "text": "plus cos square theta plus two sine theta into cos theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.68,
      "end": 34.559,
      "text": "is equal to forty-nine by twenty-five."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.02,
      "end": 35.739,
      "text": "Now, as we know,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.36,
      "end": 40.279,
      "text": "the standard identity sine square theta plus cos square theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.819,
      "end": 49.459,
      "text": "is always equal to one, and it works for every angle. So we replace sine square theta plus cos square theta with one."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.899,
      "end": 61.039,
      "text": "Now, the equation becomes one plus two sine theta into cos theta is equal to forty-nine by twenty-five. Now, the question is asking for the value of sine theta into cos theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.379,
      "end": 63.459,
      "text": "So we need to isolate that term."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.84,
      "end": 71.379,
      "text": "Subtracting one from both sides, we get two sine theta into cos theta is equal to twenty-four by twenty-five. Now divide both sides by two."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.68,
      "end": 76.299,
      "text": "We get sine theta into cos theta is equal to twelve by twenty-five. Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.259,
      "end": 79.239,
      "text": "So the final answer will be twelve by twenty-five."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.9,
      "end": 80.319,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 80.9,
      "end": 82.299,
      "text": "option D is the correct answer."
    }
  ],
